# The rule behind every line here:
# we commit the CODE THAT REGENERATES a file, never the file itself.

# ---- Data ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Gigabytes, and fully reproducible from scripts/ + configs/. Committing it
# once makes the repository unclonable forever, because Git keeps history.
# We keep the empty folder markers so the structure survives a clean clone.
data/**
!data/**/
!data/**/.gitkeep

# ---- Generated dataset ---------------------------------------------------
# Exception to the rule at the top of this file, made deliberately: the raw
# and intermediate data (multi-GB, see "Data" above) stays out, but the
# FINAL encoded corpus is small (~22MB total for TinyStories at vocab 8000),
# frozen since the Lesson 3 dataset review, and committing it means Colab/
# Kaggle can `git clone` and train directly - no separate upload step, no
# re-running the whole pipeline on every fresh environment.
# If the corpus ever grows past ~100MB, switch to Git LFS or Hugging Face
# Hub instead of reverting this.

# ---- Model weights (from Lesson 10 onwards) ------------------------------
checkpoints/

# ---- Secrets -------------------------------------------------------------
# The most expensive line in this file.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Python --------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ---- Notebook and editor noise -------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
